"help.title" = "How to play";
"help.done" = "Done";
"help.how.title" = "The game";
"help.how.body" = "Climb a skyscraper under construction by jumping from girder to girder, as high as you can. You can pass through girders from below and land on top of them. Girders get narrower as you climb.";
"help.controls.title" = "Controls";
"help.controls.body" = "Hold the left half of the screen to run left and the right half to run right. The faster you run, the higher you jump. Hit a wall and you bounce off it, keeping your speed.";
"help.auto.title" = "Jumping";
"help.auto.body" = "While climbing, your character jumps by itself every time it lands; you only steer. The boss fight is a separate mode: there is no auto jump, so swipe the finger you are holding upward to jump. Auto jump comes back when the fight is over.";
"help.trophy.title" = "Trophies and checkpoints";
"help.trophy.body" = "Every 100 floors you win a trophy: Bronze, Silver, Gold, Diamond, then Legend. The floor where you win it becomes your checkpoint, and your next game can start there. To start from the bottom, use \"Start over\" on the title screen.";
"help.chapters.title" = "Chapters";
"help.chapters.body" = "Each chapter is 1000 floors; girders start wide and get narrower toward the end. Floors 0-999: steel girders. Floors 1000-1999: short girders that slide left and right and carry you with them. Floors 2000-2999: slippery girders that are hard to stop on. Floor 3000 and up: all of them mixed.";
"help.boss.title" = "Bosses";
"help.boss.body" = "At the end of every chapter (floor 1000, 2000, ...) a boss is waiting, in this order: Captain Inkbeard (octopus), Professor Wriggle (worm), Count Flapwing (bat), Zorp from Space (alien in a flying saucer), Rusty Rivet (robot), and Growler the Bulldog. After the sixth, the order starts again and the bosses get tougher. During the fight the burning film stops and you cannot climb to the girders above. Your character fires upward on its own; stay under the boss to hit it. Before every attack the boss warns you (a \"!\" sign and a glow). Attacks: fans and aimed shots, a wave along the floor (jump over it), rain, rings, and bouncing pieces; beams and geysers land where the floor is marked, so get away from that spot. You have three hearts; after a hit you are briefly untouchable. Beat the boss to win 3 cups and move on to the next chapter. If you fall during the fight, your next game starts at the fight. Use the Boss fights button on the title screen to fight only bosses: all six in a row or the one you pick.";
